usage: course verify [-h] [--root DIR]
                     --status {predicted,unverified,corrected,identical,verified,written}
                     [--lab GROUP] [--station PATH] [--install DIR] [--date YYYY-MM-DD] [--json]

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --root DIR            niagara-research checkout (default: $NIAGARA_RESEARCH_DIR, then found from
                        cwd)
  --status {predicted,unverified,corrected,identical,verified,written}
                        the status of the items to decide (written = no marker)
  --lab GROUP           one group: a lab number (3 or L3), B, A, RA1, RA2, RAX, RA (all three),
                        EXAM
  --station PATH        station directory, or its config.bog (zipped or plain XML); default:
                        $COURSE_TRAINING_STATION for the labs, $COURSE_REVIEW_STATION for RA1/RA2,
                        $COURSE_CERT_STATION for EXAM
  --install DIR         Niagara install whose modules/ holds the built jars (default:
                        $COURSE_NIAGARA_INSTALL; jar checks SKIP without either)
  --date YYYY-MM-DD     date written in the suggested *(verified live ...)* lines (default: today)
  --json                machine JSON output
